  levelId: level_83
  levelTitle: Beyond the Shadow
  initialPage: 0
  pages:
  - title: 01 / Wire the orbital workstation
    explanation: Connect the numbered pairs and the ten 5 V feeds. Connect W104 last.
      Test emergency isolation and the independent undervoltage channel.
    caption: "138 WIRES  \xE2\u20AC\xA2  269 FUNCTIONAL SOCKETS"
    parts:
    - id: input
      kind: 9
      position: {x: 0.18, y: 0.71}
      label: WIRE
      color: {r: 0.18, g: 0.86, b: 0.94, a: 1}
    - id: tracking
      kind: 9
      position: {x: 0.71, y: 0.71}
      label: POWER
      color: {r: 1, g: 0.71, b: 0.31, a: 1}
    - id: output
      kind: 9
      position: {x: 0.82, y: 0.71}
      label: TEST
      color: {r: 0.18, g: 0.86, b: 0.94, a: 1}
    wires:
    - points:
      - {x: 0.25, y: 0.71}
      - {x: 0.43, y: 0.71}
      energized: 0
      color: {r: 0.18, g: 0.86, b: 0.94, a: 1}
    - points:
      - {x: 0.71, y: 0.71}
      - {x: 0.75, y: 0.71}
      energized: 0
      color: {r: 1, g: 0.71, b: 0.31, a: 1}
  - title: 02 / Capture sunlight
    explanation: Deploy and home both wings. Measure both PV curves, enable MPPT,
      precharge, then close the main contactor. Calibrate the main bus transducer.
    caption: "DEPLOY  \xE2\u20AC\xA2  HOME  \xE2\u20AC\xA2  TRACK"
    parts:
    - id: input
      kind: 9
      position: {x: 0.18, y: 0.71}
      label: DEPLOY
      color: {r: 0.18, g: 0.86, b: 0.94, a: 1}
    - id: tracking
      kind: 9
      position: {x: 0.71, y: 0.71}
      label: SWEEP
      color: {r: 1, g: 0.71, b: 0.31, a: 1}
    - id: output
      kind: 9
      position: {x: 0.82, y: 0.71}
      label: REGULATE
      color: {r: 0.18, g: 0.86, b: 0.94, a: 1}
    wires:
    - points:
      - {x: 0.25, y: 0.71}
      - {x: 0.43, y: 0.71}
      energized: 0
      color: {r: 0.18, g: 0.86, b: 0.94, a: 1}
    - points:
      - {x: 0.71, y: 0.71}
      - {x: 0.75, y: 0.71}
      energized: 0
      color: {r: 1, g: 0.71, b: 0.31, a: 1}
  - title: 03 / Survive eclipse
    explanation: Commission both battery packs, scan cells and balance them. Plan
      mission loads and finish a complete orbit. Diagnose and repair each of the
      three disturbances.
    caption: "CHARGE  \xE2\u20AC\xA2  PLAN  \xE2\u20AC\xA2  SURVIVE"
    parts:
    - id: input
      kind: 9
      position: {x: 0.18, y: 0.71}
      label: STORE
      color: {r: 0.18, g: 0.86, b: 0.94, a: 1}
    - id: tracking
      kind: 9
      position: {x: 0.71, y: 0.71}
      label: SURVIVE
      color: {r: 1, g: 0.71, b: 0.31, a: 1}
    - id: output
      kind: 9
      position: {x: 0.82, y: 0.71}
      label: RECOVER
      color: {r: 0.18, g: 0.86, b: 0.94, a: 1}
    wires:
    - points:
      - {x: 0.25, y: 0.71}
      - {x: 0.43, y: 0.71}
      energized: 0
      color: {r: 0.18, g: 0.86, b: 0.94, a: 1}
    - points:
      - {x: 0.71, y: 0.71}
      - {x: 0.75, y: 0.71}
      energized: 0
      color: {r: 1, g: 0.71, b: 0.31, a: 1}
  - title: 04 / Restore the trusted bus measurement
    explanation: Arm the test under load and use Undo Last to remove W104. Reconnect
      the pair. Calibrate, verify independent safety and reset. Run a new complete
      orbit.
    caption: "W104  \xE2\u20AC\xA2  CALIBRATE  \xE2\u20AC\xA2  RESET"
    parts:
    - id: input
      kind: 9
      position: {x: 0.18, y: 0.71}
      label: LATCH
      color: {r: 0.18, g: 0.86, b: 0.94, a: 1}
    - id: tracking
      kind: 9
      position: {x: 0.71, y: 0.71}
      label: RESET
      color: {r: 1, g: 0.71, b: 0.31, a: 1}
    - id: output
      kind: 9
      position: {x: 0.82, y: 0.71}
      label: QUALIFY
      color: {r: 0.18, g: 0.86, b: 0.94, a: 1}
